// The dialect pays per name (docs/plans/2026-10-16-dialect-per-name-plan.md,
// A4): a dialect function the program never names still registers when a
// body that IS used calls it. ui_web::on_menu_action's inline body calls its
// sibling inline body ui_web::posted_event (the same fragment), js::stringify
// (another fragment's inline body) and ui::post_event (declared only); and
// <ns_ui_web>'s startup anchor (`__ui_web_registered = ui::register_host(...)`)
// takes the address of every host op body. Each must be declared and its
// body emitted, in the JIT and in a native artifact — a body nobody
// registered is MIR's "import of undefined item". No session is open, so the
// engine refuses the posted event on stderr; the host's own count still runs.
// A dialect program has no gcc oracle: the expected output is the packed madc
// before the change.
int main()
{
    ui_web::host h = {};
    ui_web::on_menu_action("save", &h);
    ui_web::on_menu_action("open", &h);
    println("posted {} running {}", h.posted, h.running);
    return 0;
}
